    "available_at": "2026-11-18T18:37:18.198685+00:00",
    "body": "EICMA 2026 • 2026 EICMA's Speed Legends Exhibit Was Not To Be Missed – See the Bikes That Paved MotoGP History\nMan Blows Over $100K on New HEMI-Powered Jeep Wrangler in 2026, Sells for $70K After 6,700 Miles\n14 photos\nPhoto: Cars&Bids\nA couple of years ago, Jeep announced that it will pull the plug on the Wrangler 392 with the aptly-called Final Edition , though due to customer demand and shifting electrification plans, the company decided to keep it in its lineup.\nTherefore, those who want a V8-powered Wrangler can buy one directly from Jeep’s official dealer network, and the offering includes the Willys 392 and the Moab 392 for the 2027 model year, which have MSRPs of $70,995 and $79,995, respectively. Or they could search the used car market for one, and that is where we found the example pictured above.\nIt is a 2025 model year Jeep Wrangler Unlimited Rubicon 392 Final Edition 4x4 , which was picked up by the seller new in April 2026. The man added a little over 6,700 miles (~10,800 km) before deciding to part ways with his SUV for unknown reasons, and he advertised it on Cars&Bids, When the gavel hit the table on November 17, 2026, the vehicle changed hands for $70,199, thus leaving a toll on the seller’s finances.\nThat’s because the man paid $107,575 for his V8-powered Jeep Wrangler a little over half a year ago, so he lost $37,376 in just seven months. Thus, the ride ended up costing him over $5.5 per mile, excluding the gasoline and other work that he might have poured into it.\nPhoto: Cars&Bids This Jeep Wrangler is finished in Granite Crystal Metallic Clear Coat, has a black interior, and a clean Florida title. It has never been involved in an accident, and comes with the Customer Preferred Package 27J, Heavy Duty Full Flooring System, Off-Road Plus mode, Tru-Lok front and rear axles, and Sky One-Touch power top.\nMoreover, it also features quarter window storage bags, heavy-duty rock sliders with step assist, a transfer skid plate, removable quarter windows, power-adjustable and heated front seats, a 12.3-inch touchscreen display (Uconnect5), and an Alpine sound system.\nThere are no flaws mentioned in the listing, which reveals that the engine oil and filter were changed in September 2026, at 4,952 miles (7,969 km), and that the vehicle is accompanied by two keys, the owner’s manual, and the window sticker.\nPower comes from a 6.4-liter HEMI V8 , making 470 hp (477 ps/350 kW) and 470 lb-ft (637 Nm) of torque, which drives all four wheels through an 8-speed automatic transmission, and a 2-speed transfer case.\nThis was definitely a great deal for the new owner, who got an almost-new V8-powered Wrangler that features a lot of extras for almost $40K less. Would you have bought this jeep for $70,199 if you had the chance? After you drop a few lines below, feel free to check it out in more detail here on the quoted website.\nLiked the article? Follow us to see more stories from autoevolution in your Google feeds.\nJeep Wrangler Jeep Wrangler v8 for sale used cars auction USA\nAbout the author: Cristian Gnaticov\nAfter a series of unfortunate events put an end to Cristian's dream of entering a custom built & tuned old-school Dacia into a rally competition, he moved on to drive press cars and write for a living. He's worked for several automotive online journals and now he's back at autoevolution after his first tour in the mid-2000s. Full profile\nUP NEXT 1978 GMC Birchaven Motorhome Is a Superb Time Capsule in Perfect Working Order",
